    <briefdescription>
<para>C++ header file with the declaration of the µTest++ stopwatch. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header provides the <computeroutput>stopwatch</computeroutput> class, used to measure the elapsed time of the test suites and of the test session within the µTest++ framework. The stopwatch is started before the measured operation, stopped after it, and then reports the elapsed time as a <computeroutput>std::chrono::microseconds</computeroutput> duration.</para>
<para>Timing support relies on <computeroutput>clock_gettime(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, ...)</computeroutput> on POSIX platforms and on <computeroutput>timespec_get(..., TIME_UTC)</computeroutput> on Windows. If no clock is available (e.g. on bare-metal targets without an RTC), the readings remain zero, <computeroutput>has_elapsed()</computeroutput> returns <computeroutput>false</computeroutput>, and no timing information is reported.</para>
<para>All definitions reside within the <computeroutput><ref refid="namespacemicro__os__plus_1_1micro__test__plus_1_1detail" kindref="compound">micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus::detail</ref></computeroutput> namespace, ensuring clear separation from user code and minimising the risk of naming conflicts.</para>
<para>This file is intended solely for internal use within the framework and should not be included directly by user code. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
